    "independence": "Continuum mode cos(t) follows the independently derived cold-fluid linear equations, with O(amplitude^2) nonlinear scope. Mesh sweep keeps particle coordinates/count and dt fixed (ppc therefore varies explicitly); time sweep keeps mesh and particle coordinates fixed. DOP853 integrates exactly the same particle-grid RHS and is independent only as a time integration algorithm; its max-step sensitivity is measured. Random-load shot-noise ensembles vary only N at fixed mesh, measured at t=0, and are separate from quiet-start mesh/time errors. Analytic E[|mean exp(ix)|^2]=1/N tests particle loading; actual CIC grid mode obeys N E[|rhohat_1/grid|^2]=(2+cos(2*pi/grid))/3. Both normalized mean powers use the predeclared 0.5..1.5 bounds and their RMS reduction uses the same minimum 1.3, validating initial noise rather than evolved-plasma convergence. Gauss diagnostics exclude the real skew derivative's Nyquist null mode and separately bound that charge component."
